From 37a5a53f90f5dc2799803c2bca757a92a5d1fb2f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lance <Gero3977@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 06:05:36 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 10/22] ASoC: codecs: wcd934x: program the HPH over-current
 settings

The driver enables HPH over-current detection when the PA powers up but
never sets RX_OCP_CTL or HPH_OCP_CTL, so detection runs from the reset
values, 0x1f and 0x28. The downstream driver sets both when it
initialises the codec: two retry attempts in RX_OCP_CTL and 0x3a in
HPH_OCP_CTL, which also leaves the OCP state machine enabled. Here that
bit stays off until the first over-current interrupt toggles it.

On the LG V30, music on the HPH path at 52% volume into a 23 ohm headset
raised about 30,000 over-current interrupts per side in 13 seconds and
was heard as static. Very quiet tones raised none.

Prior art and credits: the values come from tavil_codec_reg_defaults[] in
the Qualcomm/LG msm8998 kernel, sound/soc/codecs/wcd934x/wcd934x.c.

TEST ONLY until the over-current count is measured on hardware.

Signed-off-by: Lance <Gero3977@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: Claude-Code:claude-opus-5-5
---
 sound/soc/codecs/wcd934x.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/wcd934x.c b/sound/soc/codecs/wcd934x.c
index 1da149e07..69f0ae2ca 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/wcd934x.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/wcd934x.c
@@ -2229,6 +2229,10 @@ static void wcd934x_hw_init(struct wcd934x_codec *wcd)
 
 	/* Take DMICs out of reset */
 	regmap_update_bits(rm, WCD934X_CPE_SS_DMIC_CFG, 0x80, 0x00);
+
+	/* HPH over-current: two attempts, and the downstream limit setting */
+	regmap_update_bits(rm, WCD934X_RX_OCP_CTL, 0x0f, 0x02);
+	regmap_write(rm, WCD934X_HPH_OCP_CTL, 0x3a);
 }
 
 static int wcd934x_comp_init(struct snd_soc_component *component)
